      "hints": [
        "Find $x$-intercept $(6, 0)$ from $3 + \\frac{12}{2 - x} = 0$.",
        "Differentiate $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{12}{(2 - x)^2}$.",
        "Form tangent equation using gradient at $x = 6$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the $x$-intercept of the curve $y = 3 + 12(2 - x)^{-1}$ by setting $y = 0$:\n$$3 + \\frac{12}{2 - x} = 0 \\implies \\frac{12}{2 - x} = -3 \\implies 2 - x = -4 \\implies x = 6 \\implies (6, 0)$$",
        "Differentiate the curve equation with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 12(-1)(2 - x)^{-2}(-1) = \\frac{12}{(2 - x)^2}$$",
        "Evaluate the tangent gradient at $x = 6$:\n$$m_T = \\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=6} = \\frac{12}{(2 - 6)^2} = \\frac{12}{16} = \\frac{3}{4}$$",
        "Write the equation of the tangent line at $(6, 0)$:\n$$y - 0 = \\frac{3}{4}(x - 6) \\implies y = \\frac{3}{4}x - \\frac{9}{2} \\quad \\left(\\text{or } 3x - 4y = 18\\right)$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
